 ```sh
 npm start        # http://localhost:3000, data in tasks.db (PORT and DB_PATH change them)
 npm test         # the API tests (node:test)
 ```
 
+## Accounts and authentication
+
+Each person has an account and only ever sees and changes their own tasks.
+
+1. `POST /api/users` with `{ "username", "password" }` creates an account.
+2. `POST /api/sessions` with the same body signs in and answers `{ "token": "…" }`.
+3. Every `/api/tasks` request carries `Authorization: Bearer <token>`.
+4. `DELETE /api/sessions` (with the header) signs out: the token stops working.
+
+| Method and path | Answers |
+|---|---|
+| `POST /api/users` | 201 `{ "id", "username" }`; 400 `{ "error": "invalid username" }` or `{ "error": "password too short" }`; 409 `{ "error": "username taken" }` |
+| `POST /api/sessions` | 201 `{ "token" }`; 401 `{ "error": "invalid credentials" }` (the same for a wrong username and a wrong password) |
+| `DELETE /api/sessions` | 204; 401 `{ "error": "authentication required" }` |
+
+- A username is lowercased, then must be 3 to 32 characters among `a-z`, `0-9` and `_`. Names are unique, in any case.
+- A password has at least 10 characters.
+- A missing, malformed or unknown token on a `/api/tasks` route answers 401 `{ "error": "authentication required" }`.
+- A task belongs to the user who created it. Reading, changing or deleting another user's task answers 404
+  `{ "error": "task not found" }`, exactly as for a task that does not exist.
+- Tasks created before accounts existed stay in the database (their `user_id` is `NULL`); no user sees them.
+
+Storage and security notes:
+
+- Passwords are stored as a random 16-byte salt and a scrypt hash (`node:crypto`), compared in constant time. An unknown
+  username costs the same scrypt computation as a wrong password.
+- A token is 32 random bytes from the OS (`crypto.randomBytes`), base64url encoded; only its SHA-256 is stored. Tokens
+  do not expire; they end at sign-out.
+- No response contains a password, a hash or a `user_id`.
+- There is no rate limiting on sign-in and no HTTPS in the app itself: put it behind a reverse proxy that does both
+  before exposing it. The page keeps the token in `localStorage`.
+- Request bodies are limited to 64 KiB.
+
 ## API
 
 Every body is JSON. A task is `{ "id": 1, "title": "Buy milk", "done": false, "created_at": "2026-01-31T09:00:00.000Z" }`.
+The task routes need the bearer token described above and only concern the signed-in user's tasks.
 
 | Method and path | What it does | Answers |
 |---|---|---|
 | `GET /api/tasks` | Lists the tasks, oldest first; `?done=true` or `?done=false` keeps the done or the open ones | 200, an array of tasks |
 | `POST /api/tasks` | Creates a task from `{ "title": "…" }` | 201, the task |
 | `GET /api/tasks/:id` | Reads a task | 200, or 404 `{ "error": "task not found" }` |
 | `PATCH /api/tasks/:id` | Changes `title` and / or `done` | 200, the task, or 404 |
 | `DELETE /api/tasks/:id` | Deletes a task | 204, or 404 |
 
-Errors answer `{ "error": "<message>" }`.
+Errors answer `{ "error": "<message>" }`: 400 for an invalid body, 401 without a valid token, 404, 405, 413 for a body over
+64 KiB.
 
